Package: beamline-tango-devices
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 python3.12,
Description: Tango device servers of the beamline lab, with their own runtime
 The beamline lab's five Tango device servers (magnet power supply, Ce:YAG
 camera, Faraday cup, vacuum gauge, interlock monitor) and its Sardana
 controllers, in a self-contained, hash-locked Python environment under
 /opt/beamline-tango (PyTango, pymodbus, Sardana). It ships systemd template
 units for the servers and for Sardana's Pool and MacroServer; installing the
 package enables and starts nothing.

Package: beamline-tango-simulators
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 beamline-tango-devices (= ${source:Version}),
 socat,
Description: protocol simulators for the beamline lab's Tango device servers
 Fake instruments speaking each device's real protocol (RS-232 over a socat
 pty pair, TCP/IP, GPIB through a Prologix adapter, Modbus TCP), on 127.0.0.1
 or ptys only, with systemd template units. A site with real instruments
 installs beamline-tango-devices alone.
